 # Slowreel - design
 
 ## The idea
-**Slowreel is an ambient tape machine you could hold.** One instrument, built like a high-end synth: a light painted-aluminium
-chassis, plastic keycaps in four signal colours, real knobs with skirts and indicator lines, VU needles, and a reel-to-reel
-transport behind dark glass. Everything you *touch* is light and matte; everything that *shows the sound* (counter, deck,
-VU, song cloud, song waveform) sits behind dark glass. That single contrast is the whole visual system.
+**Slowreel is an ambient tape machine you could hold, seen at night through a rainy window ("Rain glass").** One
+instrument, built like a high-end synth: a dark blue-grey clay chassis, frosted-glass keycaps and panels, real knobs with
+skirts and indicator lines, VU needles, and a reel-to-reel transport in a moonlit niche. Everything you *touch* is frosted
+dark glass with a faint top highlight; everything that *shows the sound* (counter, deck, VU, song cloud, song waveform)
+sits behind the darkest glass and is lit in rain cyan. A faint mist and slanted rain streaks sit behind the whole room.
 
 Name: **Slowreel** (model line "SR-8 ambient tape studio"), because ambient music is tape running slowly and nothing is rushed.
 
-## Tokens (css/studio.css `:root`)
-- Surfaces: `--room #C9CECC` (the desk), `--chassis`, `--panel #EDEFED`, `--panel-hi #F7F8F7`, `--well`, lanes `--lane`/`--lane-alt`.
-- Ink: `--ink #15181A`, `--ink-2`, `--ink-3`, `--ink-4` (four steps, no pure black).
-- Glass: `--glass #1B2023`, `--glass-ink #EEF0EA`, `--glass-dim`.
-- Signal colours (keycaps, LEDs, knob arcs): `--signal #EC4E20` (play/record/export/peak), `--cobalt #2D55D2` (Space reverb,
-  focus ring), `--saffron #F2A900` (loop, Echo, song-cloud glow), `--leaf #2E9E6E` (on/saved).
-- Track colours: 8 inks in `sample-project.js` `TRACK_COLORS`; each track's colour runs through its head chip, clips, notes,
-  meter, mixer strip and keyboard.
+## Tokens (css/studio.css `:root`, `color-scheme: dark`)
+- Surfaces: `--room #090E12` (the night room, misty gradients + rain streaks on `body`), `--chassis`, `--panel #131B21`,
+  `--panel-hi #19232A`, `--well`, lanes `--lane`/`--lane-alt`. Modules are slightly translucent frosted gradients.
+- Ink: `--ink #E2ECF0`, `--ink-2`, `--ink-3`, `--ink-4` (moonlit, four steps; ink-3 >= 5:1, ink-4 >= 4.5:1 on panels).
+- Glass: `--glass #060A0D`, `--glass-ink #DDF3F7`, `--glass-dim`.
+- Signal colours: `--signal #5ED6E6` rain cyan (play, export, playhead, LEDs; text on it is `--signal-ink`), `--alert #FF7A86`
+  rose (record, peak, errors), `--cobalt #8FB2FF` moonlight (Space reverb, focus ring), `--saffron #F0C674` lamp gold
+  (loop, Echo, mute), `--leaf #5BD6A8` mint (saved/done). Lit keys (selected tab, Play, pressed options) use
+  `--key-on-top/bot`, `--key-on-ink` and `--key-on-shadow`: cyan-tinted glass with a soft glow.
+- Track colours: 8 inks in `sample-project.js` `TRACK_COLORS` stay the stored data; on screen every track colour goes
+  through `ink()` (its "rain ink", a lighter misty version of the same hue that reads on dark). Clip name strips use
+  dark text on the lit colour.
+- 3D deck (`js/ui3d/scene3d.js`): dark blue-grey clay with a cool moonlit sheen, moonlight key light, a pale teal lamp in
+  the niche, brushed aluminium reels, a dark-faced cyan VU, a rainy night-city window; the knob halos glow cyan,
+  moonlight and pale white.
 - Type: Archivo (wide-ish grotesk, 600-800 for names, uppercase tracked 10px labels) + IBM Plex Mono for every number.
